accTitle: Monitoring signals and evidence boundaries
accDescr: Configuration checks, VNet flow records, resource diagnostics, connection probes, and Defender interpretation answer different questions. Only correlated live observations could prove a real path. This update has no live Azure evidence.
CFG["Terraform source<br/>Schema + mock assertions"]:::config --> C["Configuration evidence<br/>Intended values and relationships"]:::config
V["VNet traffic"]:::network --> FL["VNet flow logs<br/>Storage + optional analytics"]:::signal
R["Firewall / gateway / service"]:::network --> DL["Diagnostic categories<br/>Log Analytics"]:::signal
P["Configured probe source<br/>Agent/prerequisites required"]:::network --> CM["Connection Monitor<br/>Reachability and latency"]:::signal
FL & DL & CM --> E["Correlate source + destination<br/>Identity • timestamp • selected route<br/>Expected result vs observation"]:::evidence
C -.->|"Does not establish live traffic"| E
D["Defender findings<br/>Design worksheet only"]:::note --> W["Explain exposure and remediation<br/>Synthetic example, no assessment"]:::note
E --> N["Current Azure evidence<br/>NOT RUN"]:::note
W ~~~ N
